{
  "sources": [
    "Coal: 1936 output by country, district and state, from the U.S. Bureau of Mines Minerals Yearbook 1937 (world coal and lignite by countries; U.S. bituminous and anthracite by state) and the League of Nations Statistical Year-Book 1937/38. A point is about 5 million tonnes of hard coal, lignite at about a third; each country's sum follows P6 spec §16.1 (USA 70, Germany 45, the UK 40, the USSR 25, France, Japan, Poland and Czechoslovakia 8 to 12, the others 1 to 5), at most 8 a region.",
    "Uranium: the eight mines of P6 spec §16.1 (Shinkolobwe counts for Belgium).",
    "Hydro: the hydro-electric areas of P6 spec §16.1 in service by 1936, sized by their 1936 output; Italy's Alps about 12 and Japan about 15 (spec §16.2). The dams of landmarks1936.json give their own energy.",
    "noData: the modern countries of the Korean Peninsula and Taiwan hold no version 5 data (P6 spec §24-3, plan decision 33; no Sup'ung, Hŭngnam or Hashima)."
  ],
  "noData": ["KOR", "PRK", "TWN"],
